-> Host Discovery:

    => Host discovery determines which systems are reachable or appear to be active.

    => Ping Scan:

            nmap -sn 192.168.56.0/24

        *** '-sn' performs host discovery without performing a port scan.

        *** This is useful for creating an initial inventory of active systems.

=> Scan all ports of a target:    # nmap -p- X.X.X.X

=> Scan a specific port:          # nmap -p80 X.X.X.X

=> Scan for a set of ports:       # nmap -p80,443,21 X.X.X.X

=> Scan using a script:           # nmap -p80 --script=<script_name> X.X.X.X/domain_name

**** In Kali linux there are a collection of scripts that can be used. The location is /usr/share/nmap/scripts directory.

